{"data": [{"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2113729679127719936"]}, "author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-23T20:30:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113729745636741327"], "id": "2113729745636741327", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 5051, "like_count": 7, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "When grocery and energy bills soar, how can governments best protect the vulnerable? Keeping prices down for everyone is costly and often benefits wealthier households. In this Analytical Corner, Chiara Maggi explains a better way: https://t.co/iHRM8fTtiI https://t.co/xVy8Oc9Xzx", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2113729745636741327"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113724902306115584"]}, "author_id": "825088493764407298", "created_at": "2026-10-23T20:28:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113729267418956201"], "id": "2113729267418956201", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 18, "impression_count": 4494, "like_count": 138, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 22, "retweet_count": 15}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113718905562862065", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Last month a large team of agents used over 100 billion tokens to resolve the Navier-Stokes Millennium Prize problem. Now we're using a similar approach for red-teaming to find and fix infra vulnerabilities. https://t.co/MHH9kxLN3G https://t.co/zuTByFSQuy", "url": "https://x.com/polynoamial/status/2113729267418956201"}, {"author_id": "26538229", "created_at": "2026-10-23T20:16:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113726339987714141"], "id": "2113726339987714141", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 12457, "like_count": 16, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "Now available: Weekly data on the H.8 release, Assets and Liabilities of Commercial Banks in the United States #FedData https://t.co/WeJhdaARrt", "url": "https://x.com/federalreserve/status/2113726339987714141"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-23T19:17:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113711426070024502"], "id": "2113711426070024502", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 4183, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113632226659139918", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "This morning, two minutes after the data release, @econvitals released some highlights and charts.\n\n--Sentiment flat but above expectations.\n--Inflation expectations unchanged and at expectations https://t.co/KXL50JYZHs", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2113711426070024502"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113693953484533760"]}, "author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-23T18:08:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113693956340842508"], "id": "2113693956340842508", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 15025, "like_count": 63, "quote_count": 10, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "Another example from the WSJ of domestic politics shaping economic policy.\nThis is part of a broader geo-economic shift where national security, geopolitics, and local politics increasingly influence economic outcomes.\n#economy #markets #tariffs #geoeconomics @WSJ https://t.co/rRMZjz1NFZ", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2113693956340842508"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-23T17:19:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113681838611087572"], "id": "2113681838611087572", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 57, "impression_count": 20784, "like_count": 456, "quote_count": 14, "reply_count": 107, "retweet_count": 22}, "text": "As the gap between the internal models at the AI labs and the ones they release grow (due to safety concerns &amp; research advantages), it will be increasingly tempting for OpenAI &amp; Anthropic to exploit that advantage directly by entering new markets, especially in finance &amp; biotech", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2113681838611087572"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113676849490591744"]}, "author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-23T17:01:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113677089803260226"], "id": "2113677089803260226", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 10413, "like_count": 35, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 12}, "text": "New IMF analysis measures financial repression across 17 advanced economies over a century. It finds a postwar peak, a retreat with liberalization, and a renewed rise since the global financial crisis. Watch the full Analytical Corner: https://t.co/BvlYbPGiUZ https://t.co/IjzYBRVmbK", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2113677089803260226"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113673985359540224"]}, "author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-23T16:48:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113674028271427598"], "id": "2113674028271427598", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 13071, "like_count": 16, "quote_count": 10, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "In the latest edition of Foreign Affairs (link below).\n\nhttps://t.co/OzpV8SVQSQ\n\n#economy #markets #ai #tech #ArtificialIntelligence https://t.co/KALhqXquIl", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2113674028271427598"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113667391678816256"]}, "author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-23T16:45:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113673086256177479"], "id": "2113673086256177479", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 181, "impression_count": 53363, "like_count": 299, "quote_count": 12, "reply_count": 12, "retweet_count": 88}, "text": "I'm thrilled to be launching Econvitals today. It's been the main way in which I have been tracking and understanding the economy over the last several months. And I decided I might as well share it with all of you--for free.\n\nHas a combo of website, email lists &amp; social media. https://t.co/W5zoX7UiC4", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2113673086256177479"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113652277051269120"]}, "author_id": "612896910", "created_at": "2026-10-23T15:30:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113654179054887212"], "id": "2113654179054887212", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2504, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Employment up in the nation, down in the District of Columbia, December 2024 to December 2025 #BLSData https://t.co/OHZlthmnJ0 https://t.co/j7x1iVvCPy", "url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2113654179054887212"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113653575100313600"]}, "author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-23T15:27:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113653579139428412"], "id": "2113653579139428412", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 16370, "like_count": 95, "quote_count": 11, "reply_count": 21, "retweet_count": 30}, "text": "Final Sept UMich survey takeaways:\n• Sentiment slipped versus initial estimates.\n• Current conditions sank to 2nd-lowest on record, though expectations improved.\n• 1-yr inflation expectations edged higher to 4.7%. (Unlikely to prompt a Fed hike next week, but cements odds for https://t.co/FoeFLmxqZk", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2113653579139428412"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113639159881449472"]}, "author_id": "321536046", "created_at": "2026-10-23T14:30:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113639169931035022"], "id": "2113639169931035022", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 625, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "We’re hiring! For these positions: \n\nIT Specialist (Policy and Planning)\nhttps://t.co/curzbIOLJc\n \nIT Specialist (OS)\nhttps://t.co/ANQTYXEDRV https://t.co/XEnYpSitiD", "url": "https://x.com/BEA_News/status/2113639169931035022"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113631652719046656"]}, "author_id": "321536046", "created_at": "2026-10-23T14:00:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113631662785388592"], "id": "2113631662785388592", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 717, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "We’re hiring! For these positions:\n\nEconomist\nhttps://t.co/Rfkm3uw61I\n\nEconomist (Recent Graduate)\nhttps://t.co/A7YmTlVVC4 https://t.co/E1nT5YAAGU", "url": "https://x.com/BEA_News/status/2113631662785388592"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113627841925349376"]}, "author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-23T13:45:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113627846577209513"], "id": "2113627846577209513", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 18113, "like_count": 62, "quote_count": 11, "reply_count": 15, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "The latest from the Atlanta Fed on home affordability.  \n#economy #markets #housing #affordability @AtlantaFed https://t.co/jbBAxa213e", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2113627846577209513"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2112893870077796352"]}, "author_id": "83466368", "created_at": "2026-10-23T13:45:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113627753689833762"], "id": "2113627753689833762", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 5098, "like_count": 14, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Tune in today at 16:00 CET as Executive Board member Piero Cipollone and Professor @HowardJDavies discuss the digital euro and the future of money in the digital era with moderator @MarioPlatero.\n\nFollow live https://t.co/Z7QVhMAu6Q\n\n@festinteconomia https://t.co/QWoSH27Q8E", "url": "https://x.com/ecb/status/2113627753689833762"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-23T13:40:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113626577623826515"], "id": "2113626577623826515", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 43, "impression_count": 18872, "like_count": 254, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 130, "retweet_count": 9}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113484746999411051", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "The inventor of the term \"prompt injection\" suspects (as do I) that this may not be as large a problem in new models. This matches our tests suggesting that you can't simply prompt inject a request for higher grades in a paper, anymore. https://t.co/mmZWL9YgOt", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2113626577623826515"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113625404997009408"]}, "author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-23T13:35:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113625410864832788"], "id": "2113625410864832788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 18210, "like_count": 95, "quote_count": 6, "reply_count": 22, "retweet_count": 19}, "text": "Just as government bond yields seek to stabilize at yesterday’s lower levels, Brent crude tops $115 and WTI rises above $101 a barrel.\n(CNBC data below.)\n#economy #markets #oil #bonds #yields https://t.co/ZDwQvFZ7El", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2113625410864832788"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113617900472786944"]}, "author_id": "26538229", "created_at": "2026-10-23T13:07:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113618335065645386"], "id": "2113618335065645386", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 8, "impression_count": 23288, "like_count": 38, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "See next week's #calendar of events: https://t.co/hcpT1dsECf https://t.co/vNA8VOv7Sl", "url": "https://x.com/federalreserve/status/2113618335065645386"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113535889011867648"]}, "author_id": "83466368", "created_at": "2026-10-23T08:02:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113541608776093903"], "id": "2113541608776093903", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 6737, "like_count": 31, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 13, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "Stress tests cannot predict the next crisis, but they can reveal weaknesses and improve our capacity to prepare, says Supervisory Board member Patrick Montagner.\n\nAs risks evolve, system-wide stress testing must become broader and more agile https://t.co/jEMLAtbjbV https://t.co/Yar9kUwJVw", "url": "https://x.com/ecb/status/2113541608776093903"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113539572416016384"]}, "author_id": "83466368", "created_at": "2026-10-23T08:02:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113541550592684394"], "id": "2113541550592684394", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 6201, "like_count": 25, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 10, "retweet_count": 11}, "text": "What do consumers in the euro area expect will happen to inflation, their incomes, their spending, and the value of their homes 12 months from now?\n\nWe’ve published the latest results of our Consumer Expectations Survey.\n\nPress release https://t.co/s6xRU1g378 https://t.co/M1xdXA4C9k", "url": "https://x.com/ecb/status/2113541550592684394"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-23T06:25:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113517142880747975"], "id": "2113517142880747975", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2490, "like_count": 37, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Real estate fraudster named Elizabeth Homes", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2113517142880747975"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113503186686492672"]}, "author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-23T05:30:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113503190801092967"], "id": "2113503190801092967", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 17304, "like_count": 39, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 13}, "text": "ICYMI: Europe is weathering the energy shock better than expected, but growth remains low and fragile. Reforms for innovation, scale and resilience are key for stronger growth. Read the report:  https://t.co/uhPHeI49yY #IMFMeetings https://t.co/BvLhUSkYiJ", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2113503190801092967"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2113035966516428800"]}, "author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-23T05:05:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113497074058825773"], "id": "2113497074058825773", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 2815, "like_count": 22, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "When I’m singing the praises of Battlestar Galactica to someone who has never seen it and then someone else starts saying the ending is bad https://t.co/jTX8fcKoBG", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2113497074058825773"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113482544582631424", "3_2113482769313509377"]}, "author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-23T04:10:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113483068174692831"], "id": "2113483068174692831", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 553, "impression_count": 75136, "like_count": 1475, "quote_count": 71, "reply_count": 230, "retweet_count": 226}, "text": "By every measure, Opus 4.8 beats human experts as peer reviewers in a study of 124 Harvard social science papers covering a range from statistical analyses to formal models to qualitative work.\n\nAs academics, we need to figure out how to adapt the practice of science to AI, fast. https://t.co/a9Q1pMd6E6", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2113483068174692831"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-23T03:31:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113473403969790055"], "id": "2113473403969790055", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2133, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Memes, motifs, and slopportunities", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2113473403969790055"}], "includes": {"media": [{"media_key": "13_2113729679127719936", "type": "video"}, {"media_key": "3_2113724902306115584", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2113693953484533760", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2113676849490591744", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2113673985359540224", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2113667391678816256", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2113652277051269120", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2113653575100313600", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2113639159881449472", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2113631652719046656", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2113627841925349376", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2112893870077796352", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2113625404997009408", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2113617900472786944", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2113535889011867648", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2113539572416016384", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2113503186686492672", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "13_2113035966516428800", "type": "video"}, {"media_key": "3_2113482544582631424", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2113482769313509377", "type": "photo"}], "users": [{"id": "25098482", "name": "IMF", "username": "IMFNews"}, {"id": "825088493764407298", "name": "Noam Brown", "username": "polynoamial"}, {"id": "26538229", "name": "Federal Reserve", "username": "federalreserve"}, {"id": "279036722", "name": "Jason Furman", "username": "jasonfurman"}, {"id": "332617373", "name": "Mohamed A. El-Erian", "username": "elerianm"}, {"id": "39125788", "name": "Ethan Mollick", "username": "emollick"}, {"id": "612896910", "name": "BLS-Labor Statistics", "username": "BLS_gov"}, {"id": "321536046", "name": "BEA News", "username": "BEA_News"}, {"id": "83466368", "name": "European Central Bank", "username": "ecb"}, {"id": "1214528593", "name": "Miles Brundage", "username": "Miles_Brundage"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2113729745636741327", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlwtr703dau4xu0zlv6bcaz3lg8t", "oldest_id": "2113473403969790055", "result_count": 25}}
